BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nJoin President Koppell for his first lecture in the Am
 erican Experiment series\, where he will discuss Information\, Power\, an
 d Democracy: The First Amendment.\nThe First Amendment is the cornerstone
  of American democracy because it guarantees the fundamental freedoms req
 uired for citizens to govern themselves\, including freedom of speech\, f
 reedom of the press\, and freedom of assembly.  Citizens need access to o
 pen debate\, diverse viewpoints\, and accurate information in order to ma
 ke informed decisions. These freedoms also protect unpopular and minority
  opinions and act as a check on the state from censoring speech or contro
 lling what people learn\, think\, and say.  This lecture examines the fou
 ndational freedoms of the First Amendment and how they are applied to con
 temporary American democratic life\, including: the impact of money on ex
 pression\, the role of new media and corporate media\, the role of the pr
 ess in investigating and disseminating information\, the right to protest
  as a form of assembly and expression\, and the challenges posed by misin
 formation\, disinformation\, polarization\, fragmented media audiences\, 
 and declining public trust. At its center is a fundamental question for A
 merican democracy: What are the inherent rights and responsibilities of f
 reedom of expression in a democratic society?\n\n\n\n\n\nHosted by: Campu
 s Activities\, Civic & Voter Engagement\n\nAdditional Information can be 
 found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650840
DTEND:20261103T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T041211Z
DTSTART:20261103T193000Z
LOCATION:Presentation Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The American Experiment: Information\, Power\, and Democracy: The 
 First Amendment
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650840
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650840
X-HOSTS:Civic & Voter Engagement
END:VEVENT
